1
00:00:05,305 --> 00:00:07,540
Twenty-five years ago,
was there someone named

2
00:00:07,607 --> 00:00:09,075
Taisuke Sakura working here?

3
00:00:09,743 --> 00:00:14,314
Is the world really
so full of coincidences?

4
00:00:15,982 --> 00:00:17,884
If only you hadn't loved her,

5
00:00:18,551 --> 00:00:21,221
you wouldn't have ended up a criminal.

6
00:00:23,223 --> 00:00:24,157
KYOKO NOSE

7
00:00:24,224 --> 00:00:25,258
I understand.

8
00:00:25,325 --> 00:00:29,462
I would like to speak with you too.

9
00:00:29,963 --> 00:00:31,731
I'll be waiting.

10
00:00:46,413 --> 00:00:47,447
Mariko.

11
00:00:49,949 --> 00:00:51,084
Mariko!

12
00:01:05,465 --> 00:01:07,734
-Can I look?
-Yes.

13
00:01:10,970 --> 00:01:12,906
What? This is amazing.

14
00:01:12,972 --> 00:01:15,275
You drew this, Fusaido?

15
00:01:16,142 --> 00:01:17,110
No, uh…

16
00:01:19,279 --> 00:01:20,180
What?

17
00:01:21,147 --> 00:01:22,916
I'm Sakura.

18
00:01:23,917 --> 00:01:25,885
Taisuke Sakura.

19
00:01:26,853 --> 00:01:28,388
Sakura?

20
00:01:29,422 --> 00:01:32,125
It's such a wonderful drawing.

21
00:01:33,460 --> 00:01:35,161
I love it.

22
00:01:40,867 --> 00:01:43,636
A choice between being
a police officer or a painter…

23
00:01:43,703 --> 00:01:46,806
Oh, that's difficult.

24
00:01:47,507 --> 00:01:50,343
But you seem suited for both.

25
00:01:51,845 --> 00:01:52,912
You don't mean that.

26
00:01:52,979 --> 00:01:55,381
No, I do.

27
00:01:55,448 --> 00:01:58,485
You seem like whatever path you
decide on, you'll put in the hard work.

28
00:01:59,719 --> 00:02:00,787
I'll support you either way.

29
00:02:08,294 --> 00:02:09,662
I'm very sorry.

30
00:02:09,729 --> 00:02:10,897
I'll get some other flowers.

31
00:02:10,964 --> 00:02:13,733
-Forget that. Your hand's more important.
-I'm fine, I'm fine!

32
00:02:13,800 --> 00:02:14,734
Show me.

33
00:02:15,635 --> 00:02:17,637
That's a bit deep, isn't it?

34
00:02:18,605 --> 00:02:19,839
Let's go to the hospital.

35
00:02:48,468 --> 00:02:49,335
It's done.

36
00:03:17,697 --> 00:03:20,500
If you're expecting Mariko,
she's not coming.

37
00:03:34,681 --> 00:03:35,882
A FEW HOURS EARLIER

38
00:03:35,949 --> 00:03:36,783
Mariko.

39
00:03:37,283 --> 00:03:40,053
There's something else
I need to talk to you about.

40
00:03:42,222 --> 00:03:43,923
It's about the secret

41
00:03:44,657 --> 00:03:47,293
between me and Sayuri,
which you asked about.

42
00:03:48,328 --> 00:03:50,396
It was just before it happened with Kyoko.

43
00:03:51,030 --> 00:03:52,999
Sayuri, who was
my subordinate at the time,

44
00:03:54,601 --> 00:03:56,636
told me that Kyoko
had been acting strangely

45
00:03:57,904 --> 00:04:00,807
and that she might be seeing someone.

46
00:04:03,109 --> 00:04:06,913
I took what she said seriously
and became suspicious of Kyoko.

47
00:04:08,214 --> 00:04:09,582
In the middle of all that,

48
00:04:10,984 --> 00:04:13,453
someone attempted to kidnap you,

49
00:04:14,520 --> 00:04:17,757
and Kyoko became
extremely emotionally unstable.

50
00:04:19,592 --> 00:04:22,028
Before the culprit had even been caught…

51
00:04:25,365 --> 00:04:26,899
she got into that accident.

52
00:04:30,703 --> 00:04:32,138
After she died,

53
00:04:32,205 --> 00:04:36,009
this was found in her room.

54
00:04:38,911 --> 00:04:40,880
I thought Sayuri

55
00:04:41,514 --> 00:04:43,750
had been telling the truth.

56
00:04:44,350 --> 00:04:47,587
If it came out that Kyoko had
committed suicide after having an affair,

57
00:04:48,087 --> 00:04:50,156
it would damage the company's reputation.

58
00:04:50,823 --> 00:04:53,693
We didn't want to let the investigation
drag on any longer.

59
00:04:55,762 --> 00:04:57,964
That's what we discussed together.

60
00:04:59,065 --> 00:05:04,003
So, I asked a politician I knew
to pull some strings.

61
00:05:04,937 --> 00:05:06,172
The investigation?

62
00:05:07,073 --> 00:05:08,641
You had them call it off?

63
00:05:13,646 --> 00:05:17,684
But I started wondering if Kyoko
really could have killed herself.

64
00:05:19,052 --> 00:05:21,454
I couldn't shake the feeling
that she would never

65
00:05:22,555 --> 00:05:23,990
have died and left you behind.

66
00:05:25,158 --> 00:05:26,626
What do you mean?

67
00:05:26,693 --> 00:05:30,430
Back then, the police also considered
that it might not have been an accident…

68
00:05:33,733 --> 00:05:37,003
but a murder.

69
00:05:47,780 --> 00:05:49,315
TAISUKE SAKURA

70
00:05:50,350 --> 00:05:51,517
Yes, hello?

71
00:05:53,953 --> 00:05:55,121
Right now?

72
00:06:00,793 --> 00:06:02,328
SOTA YUKIMURA: THREE MISSED CALLS

73
00:06:03,830 --> 00:06:05,064
SOTA YUKIMURA

74
00:06:09,235 --> 00:06:10,069
Hello?

75
00:06:10,136 --> 00:06:12,772
Mariko, I'm at your house
right now. Where are you?

76
00:06:15,408 --> 00:06:16,309
Wait, don't go!

77
00:06:17,243 --> 00:06:18,511
What? What happened?

78
00:06:18,578 --> 00:06:20,279
I'll explain why later.

79
00:06:20,346 --> 00:06:21,547
Please stay at my place.

80
00:06:22,215 --> 00:06:26,652
But I already agreed I'd go see him.

81
00:06:27,286 --> 00:06:28,221
Where are you?

82
00:06:29,088 --> 00:06:30,490
It's that detective, right?

83
00:06:31,591 --> 00:06:33,126
Where did you agree to meet him?

84
00:06:33,793 --> 00:06:35,495
Is something wrong with Sakura?

85
00:06:37,430 --> 00:06:39,399
Give me an explanation!

86
00:06:42,535 --> 00:06:44,170
You're always like this!

87
00:06:44,237 --> 00:06:46,372
You never tell me the important stuff.

88
00:06:46,439 --> 00:06:47,473
Tell me!

89
00:06:50,810 --> 00:06:53,079
I-I'll tell you everything later.

90
00:06:54,747 --> 00:06:55,948
So please.

91
00:06:56,549 --> 00:06:57,917
For now, just trust me.

92
00:06:59,719 --> 00:07:00,686
Please.

93
00:07:13,933 --> 00:07:15,468
So it was you, Detective.

94
00:07:16,202 --> 00:07:17,970
You were the one
who killed Tateiwa and Sayuri.

95
00:07:19,238 --> 00:07:20,473
Why?

96
00:07:25,545 --> 00:07:29,048
Is it because they found out
about the secret from 25 years ago?

97
00:07:29,115 --> 00:07:30,616
‎FUSAIDO

98
00:07:39,192 --> 00:07:41,060
So you found out too?

99
00:07:53,406 --> 00:07:54,907
It only happened once.

100
00:07:57,510 --> 00:08:02,515
For once in my entire life,
I made a mistake.

101
00:08:04,083 --> 00:08:05,985
And I've kept it secret…

102
00:08:08,254 --> 00:08:09,889
for 25 years too.

103
00:08:11,724 --> 00:08:13,960
-Sakura, you got a call on line five.
-Okay.

104
00:08:17,463 --> 00:08:18,931
Yes, this is Sakura.

105
00:08:18,998 --> 00:08:22,835
On that day, that man called me.

106
00:08:23,336 --> 00:08:24,570
Who are you?

107
00:08:25,371 --> 00:08:27,473
He wouldn't reveal who he was.

108
00:08:28,307 --> 00:08:30,910
but he spoke as if he knew the secret…

109
00:08:33,412 --> 00:08:35,648
between me and Kyoko.

110
00:08:38,951 --> 00:08:43,756
I was waiting to see what kind
of man would show up…

111
00:08:47,393 --> 00:08:48,528
and you were there.

112
00:08:50,763 --> 00:08:55,001
I have evidence that you
obtained that partnership through fraud.

113
00:08:55,067 --> 00:08:57,069
I can use this.

114
00:08:57,970 --> 00:08:59,305
That's what I thought.

115
00:09:01,807 --> 00:09:06,646
Someone told me that you
may have been frequenting

116
00:09:06,712 --> 00:09:09,081
the Nose family home 25 years ago.

117
00:09:10,449 --> 00:09:13,386
I heard that the company president's
ex-wife, Kyoko,

118
00:09:13,452 --> 00:09:18,090
was suspected of having
an affair with a younger man.

119
00:09:19,659 --> 00:09:20,560
You…

120
00:09:22,194 --> 00:09:24,163
were the one she had an affair with,

121
00:09:24,997 --> 00:09:27,066
yet 25 years later, you showed up again

122
00:09:27,900 --> 00:09:30,102
as a potential marriage prospect
for Mariko.

123
00:09:31,137 --> 00:09:33,072
What was your goal?

124
00:09:39,312 --> 00:09:42,448
You don't need to know
anything more than that.

125
00:09:58,464 --> 00:10:01,267
Truth is, I didn't want to kill him.

126
00:10:02,401 --> 00:10:04,437
No one needs to know

127
00:10:05,271 --> 00:10:07,406
about Kyoko and me.

128
00:10:08,874 --> 00:10:12,778
But everyone kept fixating on Mariko

129
00:10:13,613 --> 00:10:15,648
and probing into our past.

130
00:10:16,382 --> 00:10:21,153
Tateiwa, Sayuri, and Yukimura.

131
00:10:22,321 --> 00:10:23,856
You too.

132
00:10:26,626 --> 00:10:29,161
If you had just quietly
taken the fall as the culprit…

133
00:10:33,599 --> 00:10:35,601
you wouldn't have had to die.

134
00:10:57,056 --> 00:11:01,827
You don't have to watch me
that closely. I'm not going anywhere.

135
00:11:03,129 --> 00:11:04,163
Sorry.

136
00:11:05,164 --> 00:11:06,832
Sota would get mad at me otherwise.

137
00:11:09,001 --> 00:11:12,338
What is he trying to do this time?

138
00:11:13,005 --> 00:11:14,674
Tomoya, didn't he tell you anything?

139
00:11:15,207 --> 00:11:17,443
Absolutely nothing!

140
00:11:17,510 --> 00:11:20,413
Then why are you helping him right now?

141
00:11:21,347 --> 00:11:22,348
Because we're friends.

142
00:11:22,415 --> 00:11:24,450
That's a kindergartner's excuse.

143
00:11:25,251 --> 00:11:26,118
Okay then.

144
00:11:27,219 --> 00:11:28,320
Want to play cards?

145
00:11:28,387 --> 00:11:29,388
-No.
-What?

146
00:11:29,455 --> 00:11:30,923
Then how about shiritori?

147
00:11:37,997 --> 00:11:41,100
Wait, wait, you probably
shouldn't look at that…

148
00:11:43,936 --> 00:11:44,870
This is…

149
00:11:47,473 --> 00:11:48,441
-Kyoko.
-Hm?

150
00:11:48,507 --> 00:11:50,176
I wanted to give you these today.

151
00:11:50,676 --> 00:11:51,777
Here.

152
00:11:51,844 --> 00:11:52,678
-What, for me?
-Yes.

153
00:12:12,064 --> 00:12:14,033
You're a lot like your mother.

154
00:12:15,434 --> 00:12:17,303
She was a quiet person,

155
00:12:18,037 --> 00:12:21,640
but she was like a sunflower
blooming in the family.

156
00:12:21,707 --> 00:12:24,310
I painted someone I loved.

157
00:12:34,620 --> 00:12:39,191
Wait. Maybe you'd better stop.

158
00:12:40,659 --> 00:12:42,561
What was Yukimura investigating?

159
00:12:43,162 --> 00:12:45,164
Tomoya, this is important!

160
00:12:45,231 --> 00:12:46,432
How is my mother involved?

161
00:12:46,499 --> 00:12:48,901
And Tateiwa and Sayuri?

162
00:12:49,535 --> 00:12:52,138
I don't really know either,

163
00:12:52,204 --> 00:12:55,007
but I think he was
investigating everything strange

164
00:12:55,074 --> 00:12:57,710
that was happening around you.

165
00:13:12,892 --> 00:13:13,826
I have to go.

166
00:13:14,560 --> 00:13:16,796
Wait, wait, wait.

167
00:13:16,862 --> 00:13:19,665
-Sota said you really had to stay here.
-Please!

168
00:13:20,166 --> 00:13:21,967
I have to protect Yukimura.

169
00:13:30,943 --> 00:13:32,144
Okay. I'm coming too.

170
00:13:38,117 --> 00:13:40,252
It's Kyoko that you see in her, isn't it?

171
00:13:41,620 --> 00:13:42,888
In Mariko.

172
00:13:44,690 --> 00:13:46,859
When I first met Mariko,

173
00:13:47,593 --> 00:13:49,528
I thought it was Kyoko
standing right there.

174
00:13:49,595 --> 00:13:51,530
I was stunned.

175
00:13:53,132 --> 00:13:54,400
She is

176
00:13:56,001 --> 00:13:58,337
the woman fate intended for me.

177
00:14:00,573 --> 00:14:02,775
Which one do you mean?

178
00:14:05,511 --> 00:14:07,079
Why did you do that to Kyoko?

179
00:14:09,615 --> 00:14:12,184
-You killed her, didn't you?
-Because I loved her.

180
00:14:14,620 --> 00:14:16,455
You understand, don't you?

181
00:14:18,557 --> 00:14:19,892
When the person you love

182
00:14:20,860 --> 00:14:24,363
doesn't love you the way you want them to,

183
00:14:25,197 --> 00:14:26,732
hatred begins to grow.

184
00:14:28,234 --> 00:14:30,870
But I regret it.

185
00:14:32,137 --> 00:14:33,939
I was young.

186
00:14:36,842 --> 00:14:39,612
So I didn't understand her situation

187
00:14:40,546 --> 00:14:42,681
or what she was going through.

188
00:14:49,088 --> 00:14:50,189
I'm sorry.

189
00:14:50,756 --> 00:14:52,358
I didn't mean it that way.

190
00:14:53,959 --> 00:14:57,763
But you said you enjoyed being with me.

191
00:14:58,697 --> 00:15:02,201
You said you wished I would
deliver flowers every day, didn't you?

192
00:15:03,135 --> 00:15:07,806
I was shaken
when she suddenly rejected me.

193
00:15:11,710 --> 00:15:17,316
She had seemed to accept me.

194
00:15:18,984 --> 00:15:23,389
I couldn't understand
why she had suddenly changed her mind.

195
00:15:24,990 --> 00:15:28,727
After that, she avoided me.

196
00:15:29,895 --> 00:15:33,098
I just wanted to talk about it with her.

197
00:15:33,799 --> 00:15:35,100
It was you.

198
00:15:37,069 --> 00:15:38,504
You kidnapped Mariko.

199
00:15:39,705 --> 00:15:40,539
Why…

200
00:15:42,975 --> 00:15:45,844
Why? Why? Why!?

201
00:15:46,478 --> 00:15:51,317
When I realized she thought I was the kind
of person who would kidnap someone…

202
00:15:54,653 --> 00:15:57,022
I lost my temper.

203
00:16:00,392 --> 00:16:01,427
Forgive me.

204
00:16:09,301 --> 00:16:14,673
But after some time had passed
and I had calmed down, I understood.

205
00:16:15,975 --> 00:16:19,144
She was much older than me.

206
00:16:20,279 --> 00:16:22,281
She had her own situation in life,

207
00:16:24,116 --> 00:16:28,320
so, of course, she couldn't accept me.

208
00:16:30,756 --> 00:16:31,890
But…

209
00:16:34,827 --> 00:16:37,830
I couldn't understand that back then.

210
00:16:40,866 --> 00:16:42,768
Don't mess with me!

211
00:16:49,508 --> 00:16:52,277
I've only heard about Kyoko
from your perspective,

212
00:16:52,344 --> 00:16:55,014
so I don't know her feelings at all,

213
00:16:55,080 --> 00:16:57,149
I don't, but…

214
00:16:58,183 --> 00:17:01,553
the Kyoko I knew
was an incredibly bright, friendly person.

215
00:17:02,087 --> 00:17:05,557
If someone regularly visited her,

216
00:17:05,624 --> 00:17:09,228
of course, she would be
polite enough to reach out

217
00:17:09,294 --> 00:17:10,963
and make them feel welcome, right?

218
00:17:12,297 --> 00:17:13,866
What are you talking about?

219
00:17:14,433 --> 00:17:16,368
She always looked at my paintings.

220
00:17:17,036 --> 00:17:18,437
They made her happy.

221
00:17:19,038 --> 00:17:20,939
She said she was my number-one fan.

222
00:17:21,573 --> 00:17:24,309
-She said she'd cheer me on!
-That's right!

223
00:17:24,376 --> 00:17:26,311
She was cheering you on!

224
00:17:26,378 --> 00:17:27,813
But nothing more!

225
00:17:29,048 --> 00:17:32,451
She was struggling with her relationship
with her husband!

226
00:17:34,787 --> 00:17:36,155
That's why I…

227
00:17:41,527 --> 00:17:42,394
Excuse me.

228
00:17:44,096 --> 00:17:45,064
Delivery.

229
00:17:47,866 --> 00:17:48,700
Here you are.

230
00:17:48,767 --> 00:17:50,369
Thank you.

231
00:17:51,670 --> 00:17:53,172
Are you okay?

232
00:17:59,978 --> 00:18:01,647
This cheers me up.

233
00:18:03,382 --> 00:18:04,850
So pretty.

234
00:18:11,557 --> 00:18:14,493
I had to protect her.

235
00:18:18,797 --> 00:18:22,301
But even assuming
Kyoko was struggling with her husband,

236
00:18:22,367 --> 00:18:24,636
that doesn't mean she loved you.

237
00:18:26,038 --> 00:18:28,273
She never asked you to save her.

238
00:18:30,109 --> 00:18:32,744
What you consider kindness
was frightening to her.

239
00:18:42,521 --> 00:18:44,223
Well, I guess I was the same.

240
00:18:48,293 --> 00:18:49,928
Even though she never asked me to,

241
00:18:51,497 --> 00:18:53,265
I thought I had to protect her
or help her.

242
00:18:57,102 --> 00:19:00,739
I never once made the mistake
of thinking she liked me, though.

243
00:19:01,807 --> 00:19:03,542
That's not true.

244
00:19:04,576 --> 00:19:07,246
I was only trying to help her.

245
00:19:09,381 --> 00:19:10,382
Forgive me.

246
00:19:11,817 --> 00:19:13,218
So…

247
00:19:14,253 --> 00:19:17,256
I didn't do anything to frighten her!

248
00:19:19,424 --> 00:19:22,294
She must have loved me.

249
00:19:24,963 --> 00:19:25,964
After all…

250
00:19:29,601 --> 00:19:32,104
After all, she's the woman
fate intended for me.

251
00:19:37,176 --> 00:19:38,010
Yukimura?

252
00:19:38,076 --> 00:19:39,211
Sota?

253
00:19:39,278 --> 00:19:40,779
Stay away!

254
00:19:43,715 --> 00:19:44,983
Yukimura…

255
00:19:51,657 --> 00:19:52,691
See?

256
00:19:54,359 --> 00:19:55,961
She came after all.

257
00:20:04,803 --> 00:20:05,971
Kyoko.

258
00:20:08,473 --> 00:20:10,209
Why are you looking at me like that?

259
00:20:12,511 --> 00:20:16,782
I just love you, that is all.

260
00:20:18,550 --> 00:20:19,718
I am…

261
00:20:21,820 --> 00:20:23,188
Mariko.

262
00:20:30,229 --> 00:20:31,496
Why…

263
00:20:36,268 --> 00:20:37,603
Stay back!

264
00:20:39,605 --> 00:20:41,240
We're the same, aren't we?

265
00:20:47,613 --> 00:20:48,814
You understand, don't you?

266
00:20:56,822 --> 00:20:57,889
Wait!

267
00:21:00,125 --> 00:21:03,395
Look, I found this
among my mother's belongings.

268
00:21:04,963 --> 00:21:07,599
I think it was meant for you, Sakura.

269
00:21:24,449 --> 00:21:28,720
Thank you
for the beautiful painting the other day.

270
00:21:28,787 --> 00:21:30,455
I'll treasure it.

271
00:21:31,456 --> 00:21:35,627
Your painting feels as though your pure,

272
00:21:35,694 --> 00:21:38,864
honest heart is reflected in it.

273
00:21:38,930 --> 00:21:40,832
It's very moving.

274
00:21:47,572 --> 00:21:49,675
I hope that you can continue to live on,

275
00:21:51,376 --> 00:21:55,047
ten years from now, 20 years from now,

276
00:21:56,315 --> 00:22:00,285
in the wonderful life that you want,

277
00:22:01,653 --> 00:22:03,322
with that same heart.

278
00:22:25,711 --> 00:22:26,945
Long time no see.

279
00:22:49,301 --> 00:22:51,903
I wonder what can change
the nature of a man.

280
00:22:55,774 --> 00:22:59,444
No, maybe it never changes.

281
00:23:01,246 --> 00:23:03,215
This man was always a straightforward,

282
00:23:04,449 --> 00:23:06,084
pure-hearted person.

283
00:23:11,390 --> 00:23:13,325
But he made some kind of mistake.

284
00:23:14,726 --> 00:23:18,730
Or maybe to him,
he had been wrong the entire time.

285
00:23:20,932 --> 00:23:22,601
Without realizing it,

286
00:23:23,235 --> 00:23:25,504
he'd reached a point of no return.

287
00:23:25,570 --> 00:23:28,140
TAISUKE ARRESTED ON SUSPICION OF MURDER

288
00:23:28,707 --> 00:23:30,809
She really is so much like her.

289
00:23:30,876 --> 00:23:35,414
In the end,
the letter from Kyoko that Mariko found

290
00:23:35,480 --> 00:23:37,349
was what made Sakura turn himself in.

291
00:23:38,583 --> 00:23:39,418
Someday…

292
00:23:39,484 --> 00:23:43,688
Through her own strength,
Mariko regained her safety.

293
00:23:44,623 --> 00:23:46,858
I just wanted to protect Kyoko.

294
00:23:52,731 --> 00:23:53,965
Mariko.

295
00:23:56,568 --> 00:23:58,570
I wanted to protect Mariko.

296
00:23:59,905 --> 00:24:03,642
I found evidence that Tateiwa
was misappropriating company expenses

297
00:24:03,708 --> 00:24:05,577
and illegally accessing
the company's system.

298
00:24:05,644 --> 00:24:09,681
I couldn't protect Mariko anymore.

299
00:24:10,315 --> 00:24:14,753
No, I never needed
to protect her in the first place.

300
00:24:14,820 --> 00:24:17,189
I figured if Mariko's safety was at risk,

301
00:24:17,856 --> 00:24:19,491
I had to do something.

302
00:24:20,091 --> 00:24:21,193
With that in mind…

303
00:24:25,797 --> 00:24:30,769
I've been watching over
Mariko Nose for 25 years.

304
00:24:32,270 --> 00:24:37,542
I wrote about Mariko and everything else
that is relevant to the case.

305
00:24:45,550 --> 00:24:47,919
We'd like to take this
as reference material

306
00:24:47,986 --> 00:24:49,554
for the investigation.

307
00:24:50,455 --> 00:24:51,389
Okay.

308
00:24:53,859 --> 00:24:54,860
What would you like to do?

309
00:24:55,727 --> 00:24:58,163
Will you file a police report
against Sota Yukimura?

310
00:25:01,032 --> 00:25:01,967
He's the man…

311
00:25:04,202 --> 00:25:07,239
who saved my daughter's life.

312
00:25:09,508 --> 00:25:11,142
I don't want him punished.

313
00:25:16,481 --> 00:25:18,483
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

314
00:25:18,550 --> 00:25:20,285
-Put the PCs in here as well.
-Okay.

315
00:25:21,553 --> 00:25:24,723
Because Mariko and the president
chose not to press charges,

316
00:25:24,789 --> 00:25:27,192
I was not held criminally responsible.

317
00:25:28,927 --> 00:25:29,895
But…

318
00:25:31,096 --> 00:25:34,032
it was time for me to take
responsibility for what I'd done.

319
00:25:40,171 --> 00:25:41,806
RESIGNATION LETTER

320
00:25:45,043 --> 00:25:47,712
You said you'd explain everything later.

321
00:26:00,292 --> 00:26:02,294
My 25-year love…

322
00:26:04,262 --> 00:26:05,430
is over.

323
00:26:30,188 --> 00:26:31,523
You were straightening them up!

324
00:26:31,590 --> 00:26:35,527
Even though you know I was fixing them,
you still put them down the wrong way?

325
00:26:35,594 --> 00:26:37,195
-Yes.
-"Yes"?

326
00:26:37,262 --> 00:26:39,164
You're being annoying!

327
00:26:39,230 --> 00:26:40,365
You're one to talk.

328
00:26:45,904 --> 00:26:48,039
When did I go wrong?

329
00:26:57,882 --> 00:26:58,817
I see.

330
00:27:00,452 --> 00:27:01,586
I guess, from the beginning…

331
00:27:19,304 --> 00:27:20,705
She was trying to do something bad.

332
00:27:22,107 --> 00:27:23,208
It can't be helped.

333
00:27:37,022 --> 00:27:40,058
The last time I spoke to Sayuri…

334
00:27:41,760 --> 00:27:44,362
she bowed and asked me
to take care of you.

335
00:27:47,966 --> 00:27:51,569
Now that we can't hear her
tell her own story anymore,

336
00:27:51,636 --> 00:27:53,338
I don't know what's true.

337
00:27:54,773 --> 00:27:55,707
But

338
00:27:56,307 --> 00:27:59,144
one thing I know for sure
is that she cared deeply about you

339
00:28:00,645 --> 00:28:04,115
and wanted you to be happy.

340
00:28:09,654 --> 00:28:11,790
This house hasn't exactly been

341
00:28:12,891 --> 00:28:16,695
a comfortable place for you two, has it?

342
00:28:18,697 --> 00:28:20,832
Thinking I had to protect you,

343
00:28:21,399 --> 00:28:23,668
I kept acting behind the scenes,
on my own.

344
00:28:24,769 --> 00:28:29,140
I never told either of you
anything that actually mattered.

345
00:28:31,142 --> 00:28:34,379
I care about both of you, Mariko…

346
00:28:36,915 --> 00:28:38,383
and you, Keito,

347
00:28:39,784 --> 00:28:41,753
more than anyone.

348
00:28:43,722 --> 00:28:45,356
You're both adults now.

349
00:28:46,291 --> 00:28:48,760
Maybe you don't need me anymore.

350
00:28:50,829 --> 00:28:54,432
But I want this to be a place
you can always come back to.

351
00:29:00,038 --> 00:29:01,439
Hear that?

352
00:29:02,307 --> 00:29:03,374
What?

353
00:29:04,008 --> 00:29:05,410
You too.

354
00:29:05,977 --> 00:29:07,412
Don't act like you're the only one
who's grown up.

355
00:29:07,479 --> 00:29:09,080
I am an adult.

356
00:29:09,681 --> 00:29:12,984
How about I make dinner tonight?

357
00:29:14,886 --> 00:29:17,956
-Mariko, you'll eat with us, right?
-Yes.

358
00:29:18,022 --> 00:29:19,390
I'll help.

359
00:29:20,525 --> 00:29:21,793
I'll help too.

360
00:29:28,366 --> 00:29:31,102
-Where should I put these?
-Hm? Oh, just there's fine. Okay, Grandma.

361
00:29:33,004 --> 00:29:36,007
-Let's do this for now.
-Yes.

362
00:29:36,074 --> 00:29:38,643
ONE YEAR LATER

363
00:29:38,710 --> 00:29:40,411
-Here?
-Here.

364
00:29:40,478 --> 00:29:41,613
-Over here.
-Yes.

365
00:29:41,679 --> 00:29:44,182
-What do you think?
-For this, is this part okay?

366
00:29:44,249 --> 00:29:45,617
-Or…
-I'm not sure.

367
00:29:45,683 --> 00:29:47,952
-Yeah. Like that is good.
-Move it a little bit forward.

368
00:29:48,019 --> 00:29:49,020
Like this? How's this?

369
00:29:51,089 --> 00:29:52,690
Okay, here we go.

370
00:29:52,757 --> 00:29:56,928
Three, two, one, start.

371
00:29:57,495 --> 00:29:58,997
Hello!

372
00:29:59,063 --> 00:30:01,599
Welcome to the official Velel account!

373
00:30:05,036 --> 00:30:08,106
People are really pouring in.

374
00:30:08,173 --> 00:30:09,707
Thank you very much!

375
00:30:10,241 --> 00:30:15,046
It's finally launching today,
Velel's Aurelie Adieu Serum.

376
00:30:16,281 --> 00:30:17,148
MENTION ITS BEST SELLING POINT!

377
00:30:17,215 --> 00:30:21,920
This serum contains
some of the hottest ingredients right now,

378
00:30:21,986 --> 00:30:24,122
including stem cell culture
supernatant and PDRN.

379
00:30:24,689 --> 00:30:26,558
Let's show them the texture.

380
00:30:27,158 --> 00:30:30,962
-Ah, shall we try it out then?
-Yes.

381
00:30:31,029 --> 00:30:32,130
Cheers.

382
00:30:32,197 --> 00:30:34,899
-Cheers!
-Cheers!

383
00:30:34,966 --> 00:30:36,835
-All right.
-Good work, everyone!

384
00:30:38,336 --> 00:30:41,806
All right, everyone,
we've got a special menu today.

385
00:30:41,873 --> 00:30:44,843
-It's all on the house.
-Thank you very much!

386
00:30:44,909 --> 00:30:46,945
Tomoya, you keep giving us stuff.

387
00:30:47,011 --> 00:30:49,080
You'll go bankrupt, you know?

388
00:30:49,147 --> 00:30:51,049
She's telling you off.

389
00:30:51,115 --> 00:30:56,354
Okay then, Sara, I guess I shouldn't
give you a special fruit juice.

390
00:30:56,421 --> 00:30:59,490
What? No, no! Please!

391
00:30:59,557 --> 00:31:00,758
Just kidding. Let's pick one.

392
00:31:01,326 --> 00:31:02,594
What would you like?

393
00:31:04,028 --> 00:31:07,232
You've got such a great boyfriend, Izumi.

394
00:31:07,799 --> 00:31:11,069
If I get married,
I'd want someone like that too.

395
00:31:11,836 --> 00:31:14,539
Right, Mariko,
have you been looking for a partner--

396
00:31:15,039 --> 00:31:16,474
What, I can't say that?

397
00:31:18,343 --> 00:31:19,777
What do you mean?

398
00:31:20,578 --> 00:31:23,581
You don't have to treat me
like I'm fragile.

399
00:31:24,682 --> 00:31:28,586
Actually, lately I've been thinking
I'd rather just stay single.

400
00:31:29,153 --> 00:31:32,090
I don't dislike being alone
in the first place.

401
00:31:32,156 --> 00:31:33,524
I enjoy my work.

402
00:31:35,093 --> 00:31:39,430
Mariko, I'm sure you'll find
the happiness you want.

403
00:31:40,965 --> 00:31:42,567
What? Asai?

404
00:31:42,634 --> 00:31:44,235
How long have you been here?

405
00:31:44,302 --> 00:31:45,637
Listen.

406
00:31:45,703 --> 00:31:49,407
Everyone can have the life they want.

407
00:31:50,508 --> 00:31:52,543
You can have it!

408
00:31:52,610 --> 00:31:54,545
Wait, Asai, is that alcohol?

409
00:31:55,446 --> 00:31:57,548
Well, is it? Is it?

410
00:31:57,615 --> 00:31:58,716
Zucchini?

411
00:32:03,855 --> 00:32:05,390
She's putting on a brave face.

412
00:32:07,025 --> 00:32:09,594
Everyone has to go through
a breakup eventually, right?

413
00:32:12,463 --> 00:32:15,099
I'm scared, you know.

414
00:32:16,868 --> 00:32:20,838
Once I have something precious,
I start imagining the day I lose it.

415
00:32:21,439 --> 00:32:25,643
It's like a countdown begins in my heart.

416
00:32:29,047 --> 00:32:29,881
It's scary.

417
00:32:35,019 --> 00:32:36,788
But I want to be with you, Izumi.

418
00:32:40,291 --> 00:32:44,062
Even if you break up someday,
it's better to have met someone at all.

419
00:32:45,129 --> 00:32:48,132
How about we treasure
the happy times we have together?

420
00:32:50,868 --> 00:32:52,904
Shouldn't you say
we're never going to break up?

421
00:32:53,671 --> 00:32:56,240
I don't make promises
about things I can't know for sure.

422
00:32:57,775 --> 00:32:58,910
I'm leaving now.

423
00:32:58,977 --> 00:33:01,479
-See you later!
-See you.

424
00:33:38,583 --> 00:33:39,517
Good morning.

425
00:33:39,584 --> 00:33:41,386
-Ah, good morning!
-Good morning!

426
00:33:41,452 --> 00:33:42,520
Perfect timing! Come here!

427
00:33:43,287 --> 00:33:44,789
-I want to ask you something.
-Yes?

428
00:33:44,856 --> 00:33:45,556
VIDEO CALL

429
00:33:45,623 --> 00:33:48,192
If you press this, you'll be able to see
the other person while you talk.

430
00:33:48,259 --> 00:33:49,494
-Whoa!
-Like this.

431
00:33:49,560 --> 00:33:52,797
Wow! Thank you.

432
00:33:52,864 --> 00:33:54,999
-Thanks as always.
-No problem.

433
00:33:55,066 --> 00:33:57,201
-I'll be going now.
-Okay, thank you!

434
00:33:57,869 --> 00:33:59,370
-Hey, hold on!
-Here!

435
00:33:59,437 --> 00:34:01,839
-What!
-How's this?

436
00:34:01,906 --> 00:34:03,441
-Amazing!
-Are you sure? It's a lot.

437
00:34:03,508 --> 00:34:04,475
Yes, it's okay!

438
00:34:04,542 --> 00:34:06,010
-Wow, thank you!
-Hey, Yuki,

439
00:34:06,077 --> 00:34:08,179
have you gotten used to life around here?

440
00:34:08,246 --> 00:34:12,784
Well, I feel really comfortable here,
like I've been here all my life.

441
00:34:13,718 --> 00:34:16,254
Like I lived here in a past life.

442
00:34:16,320 --> 00:34:17,688
I've been in this town for a year.

443
00:34:20,258 --> 00:34:23,227
The people here call me Yuki.

444
00:34:23,294 --> 00:34:24,095
TOMIYA COOPERATIVE FISH MARKET

445
00:34:24,929 --> 00:34:26,798
It's the first nickname
I've ever had in my life.

446
00:34:28,933 --> 00:34:29,867
It's not a bad feeling.

447
00:34:30,368 --> 00:34:32,370
‎REGARDING THE LOG-IN ERROR

448
00:34:33,871 --> 00:34:36,374
I thought I needed to disappear
from Mariko's world.

449
00:34:37,975 --> 00:34:42,280
I thought that meant
losing everything I had.

450
00:34:42,947 --> 00:34:45,283
Yuki! Have a drink with us! Come in!

451
00:34:45,349 --> 00:34:47,718
I can't. I have work.

452
00:34:47,785 --> 00:34:50,054
-Just one beer!
-Surprisingly, that wasn't the case.

453
00:34:50,121 --> 00:34:52,690
-Come on!
-I can live here in this town.

454
00:34:52,757 --> 00:34:55,293
This fish is delicious.

455
00:34:57,361 --> 00:34:58,463
‎Not bad, right?

456
00:35:00,798 --> 00:35:01,933
The food is great.

457
00:35:02,700 --> 00:35:03,935
The people are kind.

458
00:35:04,902 --> 00:35:06,003
It's not bad.

459
00:35:06,070 --> 00:35:08,372
That's what I'm saying!
You get it, don't you?

460
00:35:08,439 --> 00:35:09,941
I'm not sure I do.

461
00:35:10,007 --> 00:35:11,709
You have to actually say it!

462
00:35:11,776 --> 00:35:13,377
What's wrong with you all?

463
00:35:13,444 --> 00:35:16,414
My goodness, you never say
what's important out loud!

464
00:35:18,583 --> 00:35:20,985
-You know…
-You never put it into words.

465
00:35:21,052 --> 00:35:21,953
Now, now…

466
00:35:26,557 --> 00:35:30,761
I didn't think there'd be anything worth
writing in a diary anymore.

467
00:35:30,828 --> 00:35:34,765
But it turns out you can find things
worth remembering everywhere.

468
00:36:23,147 --> 00:36:26,751
She looks like Mariko.

469
00:36:34,358 --> 00:36:36,928
Am I finally hallucinating?

470
00:36:42,867 --> 00:36:44,435
That's really her, isn't it?

471
00:36:45,169 --> 00:36:46,604
What is Mariko doing here?

472
00:36:47,338 --> 00:36:50,174
There's no way a coincidence
like this could happen in my life.

473
00:36:50,241 --> 00:36:52,577
This is crazy. This is bad!

474
00:36:53,077 --> 00:36:54,178
She'll think I'm still following her!

475
00:37:06,490 --> 00:37:08,859
-I'm sorry.
-I'm sorry.

476
00:37:08,926 --> 00:37:10,795
I told you to watch out.

477
00:37:12,630 --> 00:37:13,464
What?

478
00:37:13,531 --> 00:37:15,967
-Why? Why? Why are you here?
-A coincidence.

479
00:37:16,033 --> 00:37:17,768
-Really, it's a coincidence.
-What?

480
00:37:17,835 --> 00:37:20,404
-There's no way this is a coincidence!
-There is!

481
00:37:20,471 --> 00:37:22,173
What are you doing here, Mariko?

482
00:37:23,074 --> 00:37:25,343
Well, there's a golf course near here.

483
00:37:25,409 --> 00:37:27,311
I used to visit it with my father.

484
00:37:29,513 --> 00:37:30,881
Wait, what about you?

485
00:37:30,948 --> 00:37:31,849
What are you doing here?

486
00:37:34,819 --> 00:37:37,989
I'm… living here.

487
00:37:41,125 --> 00:37:42,326
What?

488
00:37:45,129 --> 00:37:46,364
See you.

489
00:38:36,180 --> 00:38:37,648
ADHESIVE BANDAGE

490
00:38:39,317 --> 00:38:41,285
FESTIVAL

491
00:38:41,352 --> 00:38:42,286
ENTRANCE EXAM ADMISSION TICKET

492
00:39:47,418 --> 00:39:48,252
Mariko!

493
00:39:53,791 --> 00:39:59,830
You are my first love
and the person I admire.

494
00:40:02,032 --> 00:40:04,468
And you've given me a lot of happiness.

495
00:40:06,470 --> 00:40:07,571
As long as…

496
00:40:09,640 --> 00:40:11,509
you were just there,

497
00:40:12,610 --> 00:40:14,311
I didn't need anything else.

498
00:40:16,847 --> 00:40:19,049
That alone made me happy.

499
00:40:21,285 --> 00:40:22,453
But, to be honest,

500
00:40:23,821 --> 00:40:24,655
I was hoping

501
00:40:25,156 --> 00:40:28,859
we'd eventually meet by coincidence,
and we'd become close and be able to talk.

502
00:40:29,627 --> 00:40:32,763
Somewhere in my heart,
I think I was hoping

503
00:40:33,864 --> 00:40:35,366
for something like fate.

504
00:40:37,301 --> 00:40:39,737
Something that convenient
would never happen to me, of course.

505
00:40:40,504 --> 00:40:44,975
I thought I'd just keep living my life
how I have been.

506
00:40:49,947 --> 00:40:51,048
But then one day,

507
00:40:52,516 --> 00:40:56,754
I thought you might
actually get married someday,

508
00:40:56,821 --> 00:40:58,656
and I couldn't just sit still.

509
00:40:59,723 --> 00:41:01,625
I ended up impulsively talking to you.

510
00:41:04,462 --> 00:41:07,731
The real you is more careless
than I expected,

511
00:41:08,399 --> 00:41:10,901
and I never know what you're thinking.

512
00:41:13,404 --> 00:41:17,408
But even more than when I was
just watching you on social media,

513
00:41:17,475 --> 00:41:19,910
even more than when I was
making up my own version of you,

514
00:41:20,811 --> 00:41:24,381
after getting to know the real you,

515
00:41:25,115 --> 00:41:28,752
I came to love you much, much more.

516
00:41:36,093 --> 00:41:37,061
I loved you.

517
00:41:38,128 --> 00:41:41,298
I'd always loved you, for 25 years.

518
00:41:42,900 --> 00:41:45,903
I was always selfish,
and I made mistakes and everything.

519
00:41:47,805 --> 00:41:49,940
But the fact that I fell in love with you…

520
00:41:52,543 --> 00:41:53,944
was never a mistake.

521
00:41:59,617 --> 00:42:00,751
Thank you.

522
00:42:05,089 --> 00:42:09,293
You are not my destiny.

523
00:42:11,562 --> 00:42:12,496
Correct.

524
00:42:13,631 --> 00:42:16,000
I used to think the same thing.

525
00:42:17,768 --> 00:42:21,205
That if we met by coincidence,
got along by coincidence,

526
00:42:22,640 --> 00:42:24,141
and somehow found each other,

527
00:42:25,409 --> 00:42:28,279
it would mean you were my destiny.

528
00:42:30,881 --> 00:42:32,783
But I know that's wrong.

529
00:42:35,386 --> 00:42:37,588
We can meet in some
completely unremarkable way,

530
00:42:39,223 --> 00:42:41,292
nothing special at all.

531
00:42:42,192 --> 00:42:44,194
And as we casually spend
more time together,

532
00:42:45,429 --> 00:42:49,967
we get to know each other
and have memories together.

533
00:42:50,734 --> 00:42:52,036
And then,

534
00:42:52,102 --> 00:42:55,839
after spending years,
and decades side by side,

535
00:42:56,340 --> 00:43:00,611
maybe one day we'll look back and think,
"That person really was my destiny."

536
00:43:03,347 --> 00:43:04,782
That's what I think now.

537
00:43:10,054 --> 00:43:10,955
So…

538
00:43:16,827 --> 00:43:19,063
You are not my destiny.

539
00:43:24,768 --> 00:43:25,603
Not yet.

540
00:43:29,740 --> 00:43:30,574
What?

541
00:43:42,186 --> 00:43:43,287
You dropped it.

542
00:43:47,491 --> 00:43:48,325
Wait, this…

543
00:43:49,360 --> 00:43:50,194
This is my…

544
00:43:51,395 --> 00:43:52,296
How?

545
00:43:53,831 --> 00:43:54,732
It's a secret.

546
00:43:58,335 --> 00:43:59,169
Wait!

547
00:43:59,236 --> 00:44:01,872
What kind of life are you living here?

548
00:44:01,939 --> 00:44:03,107
Are you living well?

549
00:44:03,173 --> 00:44:04,041
Well…

550
00:44:04,908 --> 00:44:08,212
I'll show you around.

551
00:44:09,380 --> 00:44:12,316
Do you think you have a choice,
like not showing me around?

552
00:44:12,983 --> 00:44:13,884
Nope!

553
00:44:13,951 --> 00:44:14,985
Subtitle translation by: Maslin Friedman
